    fields:  # bb82
      statement: "For any method call on a local variable (e.g., f.decrypt(), output.write_text()), the analyzer must produce a call or unresolved_external_call edge so IO boundary and taint-flow analyses can detect it."  # bb82
      root_cause: "Python analyzer _process_call() lines 2702-2733 only emit unresolved edges for module_imports and imports receivers. Local variables with unknown type produce no edge at all."  # bb82
      fix: "Expand the unresolved edge fallback to emit edges for any receiver that is a local variable, with confidence ~0.4."  # bb82
